# Trivy ignore file — dependency vulnerability scan
#
# Every entry MUST carry an `exp:` date so a suppression cannot become permanent.
# Format: <ID> exp:YYYY-MM-DD
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CVE-2026-14257 / GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg — brace-expansion
# "DoS via unbounded expansion length causing an out-of-memory process crash"
#
# Why this is suppressed: the vulnerability IS fixed in what we install; the
# advisory's version range is wrong. GitHub recorded a single range for this
# CVE — ">= 0, < 5.0.8" — so every patched 1.x/2.x maintenance backport still
# matches it, because 1.1.17 and 2.1.3 are semver-lower than 5.0.8.
#
# What we install (see pnpm.overrides in package.json):
#   brace-expansion 1.1.17  <- minimatch@3 (ESLint 8 chain)   patched backport
#   brace-expansion 2.1.3   <- minimatch@9                     patched backport
#   brace-expansion 5.0.8   <- minimatch@10                    advisory-clean
#
# Verified, not assumed: the maxLength / EXPANSION_MAX_LENGTH bound is present
# and enforced in each package's actual entry point, and the advisory's own PoC
# (expand('{a,b}'.repeat(1500))) returns in ~0.5s instead of OOM-crashing Node.
#
# We cannot simply move everything to 5.0.8: 5.x is ESM-first and exports only
# { expand }, while minimatch@3/@9 require a callable default export — hence the
# per-major overrides. Upgrading ESLint does not help either; eslint-plugin-react
# and eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y still depend on minimatch@3 at their latest versions.
#
# Remove this entry when the advisory is corrected — tracked upstream in
# github/advisory-database PR #8832, which splits the range per branch
# (fixed: 1.1.17 / 2.1.3 / 3.0.5 / 5.0.8). Once merged, the scan passes with no
# code change. If the expiry lapses before then, re-verify and extend
# deliberately rather than by reflex.
#
# Added: 2026-07-29
CVE-2026-14257 exp:2026-08-12
GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg exp:2026-08-12
